Grant Anderson's rehearsal in the 14th minute, converted for Frazier Climo, put the Ayrs ahead, but a yellow card for Scottish international Rory Hughes on loan for the Warriors, allowed the Melroses to take advantage of numerical superiority and Jason Baggot scored an unconverted rehearsal.
Climo extended the Ayr's advantage with a penalty and, just at half-time, scored and converted a rehearsal to put the 17-5 score in favour of the Ayr at the break.
But the Melroses started the second half well and Patrick Anderson's rehearsal, converted by Baggot, reduced the differences to five points.
Afterwards, the match was interrupted for a long time due to Ruaridh Knott's serious injury, who retired on a bunk, and at the resumption the Ayr again widened the distance with a rehearsal of Stafford McDowall converted by Climo.
Next, substitute captain Blair Macpherson was admonished with a yellow card and, again, the Melroses took advantage of the superiority of one more man with an unconverted rehearsal by Bruce Colvine at the end of a few moments of strong pressure.
However, the home team reacted and when Struan Hutchinson saw a yellow card to make a tackle to Climo without a ball, from the sanction alignment, MacPherson scored a counter-rehearsal behind Ayr's penetrating mole.
Climo scored, as he had done again almost since the resumption, after Kyle Rowe picked up a shot from David Armstrong and passed the ball in the third line to Gregor Henry to score the fifth rehearsal of the home team.
The star of the Still Game series seems to be ready to start a new career in the catering sector
Ford Kieran, star of the Still Game series, appears to be ready to move into the hospitality sector, after it has been discovered that he has been appointed director of a licensed restaurant company.
The 56-year-old actor plays Jack Jarvis' character in the popular BBC series, which he writes and co-stars with Greg Hemphill, his comic partner for a long time.
The duo have announced that the ninth season will be the last in the series, and it appears Kiernan is planning his life after Craiglang.
According to official records, he is the director of Adriftmorn Limited.
